      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HUNGRY JOE (10) won two starts ago then things went wrong last start when he broke and finished a long last over 1720m at Penrith. Has to contend with a very wide draw. Won't find this any harder so he can return to winning ways. HESAA LISTER (4) has been racing very well of late and went close again last time over 1609m at this track, finishing second and 3 metres from the winner. Tackles a similar assignment and he can bounce back to winning ways. BIRDY GAL (8) is right in contention after finishing in the placings for the second time in a row last start, beaten a nose into second at this track. No reason she cannot take this out. MICKEY BE NIMBLE (3) showed pleasing improvement last time out when third over 1609m at this track. Worth a second look.",
